<header class="ref-head"><span class="hero-ornament"></span><h1 class="research-title">19 April in history</h1><p class="ref-lede">5 events that happened on 19 April, from 1529 to 1995.</p></header>
<ol class="day-events"><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">1529 <span class="tih-ago">497 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Lutheran princes protest at the Diet of Speyer</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Six princes and fourteen imperial cities formally protested against the Diet's move to curb the Reformation. Their Protestation gave the movement the name 'Protestant'.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card tih-has-thumb tih-event-hero"><p class="tih-hero-kicker">&#10022; Anniversary of the day</p><a class="tih-event-thumb" href="/encyclopedia/boston" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/boston.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="76" height="76"></a><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">1775 <span class="tih-ago">251 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Shots at Lexington and Concord begin the American Revolution</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Militiamen clashed with British regulars at Lexington and Concord in Massachusetts, and harried them all the way back to Boston. The skirmishes began the War of Independence.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/boston">Boston</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card tih-has-thumb"><a class="tih-event-thumb" href="/encyclopedia/athens" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/athens.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="76" height="76"></a><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">1897 <span class="tih-ago">129 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">First Boston Marathon is run</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Fifteen runners set out on the first Boston race, inspired by the marathon at the 1896 Athens Olympics. It is now the world's oldest annual marathon.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/athens">Athens</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/boston">Boston</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card tih-has-thumb"><a class="tih-event-thumb" href="/encyclopedia/warsaw" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/warsaw.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="76" height="76"></a><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">1943 <span class="tih-ago">83 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Warsaw Ghetto Uprising begins</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Jewish fighters resisted German troops sent to deport the ghetto's remaining inhabitants to Treblinka. They held out for nearly a month in the largest Jewish revolt of the war.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/warsaw">Warsaw</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">1995 <span class="tih-ago">31 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Truck bomb kills 168 in Oklahoma City</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Timothy McVeigh detonated a truck bomb outside the Alfred P. Murrah Federal Building, killing 168 people, including 19 children. It remains the deadliest act of domestic terrorism in US history.</p></div></li></ol>
